FOLLOW-UP: Fee Waiver Request - Additional Grounds

Dear Public Records Officer:

I am writing to supplement my fee waiver request for the CAD record respons=
ive to my public records request. I wish to clarify two critical points tha=
t directly support waiver eligibility under Oregon public records law.

---

I AM INDIGENT

I am a volunteer caretaker living in an RV on federal land. I have no regul=
ar income. I survive through volunteer service in exchange for a place to p=
ark my RV. I do not receive wages, salary, or compensation of any kind for =
this work.

This is not a modest expense I can easily absorb-I meet the statutory defin=
ition of indigent. Requiring payment to obtain the identity of law enforcem=
ent officers who appeared at my residence creates a direct barrier to accou=
ntability for someone with zero income.

---

THIS RECORD WILL BE MADE PUBLIC

I maintain a public-interest archive at oprdvolunteerabuse.org documenting =
institutional conduct by Oregon Parks and Recreation Department and related=
 law enforcement activity. This archive serves the public interest by provi=
ding transparent, independently verifiable documentation of government acti=
ons.

The CAD record you have identified will be published in full on this archiv=
e, making it freely accessible to:
- Other volunteers navigating similar institutional circumstances
- Journalists investigating volunteer program accountability
- Legislators considering volunteer protection reforms
- Legal advocates working on related cases
- Members of the public seeking transparency in law enforcement coordinatio=
n

**This is not a personal request-it is a public records request that will r=
esult in public disclosure.** The information benefits the public, not me i=
ndividually.

---

TIMELINE MATTERS

You initially denied that any responsive records existed (April 3, 2026). O=
nly after I requested documentation of your search methodology (April 4, 20=
26) did you locate this CAD record.

I should not be charged to obtain information that:
1. You initially claimed did not exist
2. I should have been provided at the time of contact
3. Documents law enforcement officers who visited my home on restricted fed=
eral land
4. Will be published for public benefit

If you deny this fee waiver request, I will fully appeal through all availa=
ble administrative and legal channels. I am documenting every stage of this=
 process, and denial of a fee waiver under these circumstances will itself =
become part of the public record.

I am watching the clock. Please process this request expeditiously.

---

Conclusion

I meet the statutory criteria for indigence. This record serves a clear pub=
lic interest and will be made publicly available. Charging me $12.50 under =
these circumstances is neither legally required nor appropriate.

I respectfully request immediate waiver of the fee and production of the re=
sponsive CAD record.

Sincerely,

Robert Samuel White

