Subject: Re: SP26097765 - PR27478 - White

Dear Public Records Officer:

I am writing to request a waiver of the $12.50 fee associated with producin=
g the Computer-Aided Dispatch (CAD) record you have identified as responsiv=
e to my public records request.

I request this fee waiver on the following grounds:

1. Public Interest in Disclosure

This record documents law enforcement contact that occurred on restricted f=
ederal land behind a locked gate where I live and work as a volunteer caret=
aker for the U.S. Forest Service. On March 24, 2026-exactly one year after =
my dismissal from the Oregon State Parks volunteer program-three armed offi=
cers appeared at my residence: one U.S. Forest Service special agent and tw=
o Oregon State Police officers.

I was not provided the names or badge numbers of the state police officers =
at the time of contact. When I asked the USFS special agent's supervisor (C=
aptain Brandon Boyd) to identify the two state officers, he instructed me t=
o file this FOIA request to obtain that information.

The public has a significant interest in understanding:
- Under what authority state police officers accessed restricted federal la=
nd
- What coordination occurred between state and federal agencies
- Whether this contact was connected to my prior documentation of instituti=
onal conduct at Oregon State Parks
- Whether proper protocols were followed for multi-agency law enforcement c=
ontact with a civilian on federal property

2. I Am Not Seeking Commercial Gain

I am seeking this information solely to understand the circumstances of law=
 enforcement contact at my residence and to exercise my right to know the i=
dentities of officers who appeared at my door. I have no commercial interes=
t in this record.

3. Ability to Pay

I am a volunteer caretaker living in an RV with no regular income. The $12.=
50 fee, while modest, represents a meaningful expense given my current fina=
ncial constraints. More importantly, charging a fee to learn the identity o=
f officers who visited my home creates a barrier to a fundamental right.

4. I Have Every Right to Know Who Visited Me

When law enforcement officers appear at a person's residence-particularly o=
n restricted federal land where public access is prohibited-that person has=
 a basic right to know who those officers are. Requiring payment to obtain =
this information creates an unjust barrier to accountability.

The CAD record you have identified contains information I should have been =
provided at the time of contact. I should not be required to pay for inform=
ation that should have been disclosed voluntarily.

Conclusion

For the reasons stated above, I respectfully request that you waive the $12=
.50 fee and provide the responsive CAD record at no cost.

If you deny this fee waiver request, please provide a written explanation o=
f the denial and inform me of any appeal rights.

Thank you for your consideration.

Sincerely,

Robert Samuel White

